  "customimagePathTipTitle": "Enter a custom background using one of these formats",
  "customimagePathTipToggle": "View instructions",
  "customimagePathTip": "1. Relative path in the assets folder<br>e.g. assets/image.png or url(assets/image.png)<br>2. Web image URL<br>e.g. https://picsum.photos/1920/1080 or url(https://picsum.photos/1920/1080)<br>3. CSS function<br>e.g. linear-gradient(to right in oklch, #f59e0b, #06b6d4 66%, #6366f1)<br>4. Solid color<br>e.g. red, #06b6d4, oklch(from blue calc(l + 0.1) c h), color-mix(in hsl, #f59e0b, transparent)<br>5. Combine any of the above, separated by commas<br>e.g. repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent, transparent 20px, oklch(60% 0.2 10 / 0.15) 20px, oklch(60% 0.2 10 / 0.15) 40px), #8effce<br>If an image path or URL contains a comma, enclose it in quotes, for example: \"assets/a,b.png\". You can enter spaces in image paths or URLs directly.",
  "customimageBlur": "Blur",
  "customimageOpacity": "Opacity",
  "customimageEffect": "Blend Mode",
  "customimageEffectTip": "Blend mode determines how the background texture blends with the page background color<br>You may need to adjust opacity when changing the blend mode<br>1. Normal: the texture is displayed as-is without blending<br>2. Multiply: colors are multiplied, darkening the result, good for light textures<br>3. Screen: the inverse of multiply, brightening the result, good for dark textures<br>4. Overlay: darkens shadows and brightens highlights to increase contrast<br>5. Soft Light: similar to overlay but softer<br>6. Color: keeps the background brightness and applies the texture hue and saturation<br>7. Luminosity: keeps the background hue and saturation and applies the texture brightness<br>8. Color Burn: darkens the background, more noticeable with darker textures<br>9. Color Dodge: lightens the background, more noticeable with brighter textures",
